1. PERMITTED PERSONAL, COMMUNITY, STAFF, AND VENUE USE

SurroundCore may be used free of charge by individuals, charities, clubs,
organisations, public bodies, and businesses where SurroundCore itself is not
being sold, monetised, licensed, or supplied as a paid customer product or
service.

Permitted business use includes, without limitation:

- music for staff enjoyment in offices, workshops, staff rooms, warehouses,
  kitchens, back-of-house areas, and similar workplaces;
- free background or ambient music in UK pubs, restaurants, cafes, clubs, bars,
  shops, reception areas, and comparable venues;
- demonstrations, testing, development, evaluation, and internal training;
- other incidental use where customers are not paying for SurroundCore or for a
  product or service substantially based on SurroundCore.

A business earning money from its ordinary trade does not, by itself, make the
above permitted uses commercial exploitation of SurroundCore.

2. CUSTOMER-FACING COMMERCIAL AMENITIES AND EXPLOITATION

Without prior written permission from Christopher Swain, SurroundCore may not
be used where SurroundCore, or functionality substantially provided by it, is a
paid or material customer amenity, product, service, subscription, package, or
commercial offering.

For clarity, use of SurroundCore to provide in-room or guest-specific music or
entertainment in a hotel, holiday accommodation, paid hospitality package, or
similar customer accommodation is treated as commercial use and requires prior
written permission.

Other prohibited commercial exploitation includes, without limitation:

- selling, renting, licensing, sublicensing, or otherwise supplying the
  Software or a modified version for payment;
- selling hardware, appliances, systems, software packages, subscriptions, or
  services in which SurroundCore is a material part of what the customer is
  paying for;
- charging for hosted, managed, cloud, or remote access to SurroundCore;
- charging specifically for SurroundCore installation, integration,
  modification, support, maintenance, or operation as a commercial offering;
- placing SurroundCore or a derivative behind a paywall or other monetised
  access mechanism;
- using a modified, renamed, rebadged, or white-labelled version of SurroundCore
  as the basis of a commercial product or service without permission.

3. COPYING, MODIFICATION, AND REDISTRIBUTION

You may copy, modify, fork, and redistribute the Software, including modified
versions, provided you do not commercially exploit the Software contrary to
this licence and you comply with the attribution requirements below.

Redistributed copies and derived works must preserve these restrictions for all
portions derived from SurroundCore. You may not relicense those portions in a
way that permits commercial exploitation prohibited by this licence.

4. ATTRIBUTION — DO NOT PASS OFF OUR WORK AS YOURS

Any substantial copy, redistribution, modified version, public fork,
documentation, About page, credits, or derived project must retain the copyright
notice, this licence, and a clear acknowledgement substantially similar to:

    SurroundCore — created by Kev n Chris.

Equivalent wording is fine provided Kev n Chris remain clearly acknowledged.

You may describe your own modifications and contributions as your own work, but
you may not represent SurroundCore itself, or substantial work derived from it,
as having been created solely by you or another party.

5. COMMERCIAL LICENSING

Nothing in this licence prevents the copyright holder from granting separate
